From: BRL-CAD developers <devs@brlcad.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Set VERSION and SOVERSION on the mmesh shared library

The shared library libmmesh.so is currently installed without a SONAME
version number (SONAME = "libmmesh.so", same as the .so symlink name).
Well-behaved shared libraries on Linux follow the libfoo.so.MAJOR
convention so that:

 - The dynamic linker records the SONAME (libmmesh.so.1) in the
   dependent binary, not the unversioned name.
 - Multiple API versions can coexist under the same prefix without
   collisions.
 - Package managers know which .so file represents the library ABI and
   which is the development symlink.

The top-level CMakeLists.txt already declares project(mmesh VERSION 1.0.0),
so PROJECT_VERSION and PROJECT_VERSION_MAJOR are available.  We just need
to apply them to the shared library target via set_target_properties.

Applies to: BRL-CAD/mmesh, main branch (src/CMakeLists.txt)
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -12,6 +12,10 @@ if (BUILD_SHARED_LIBS)
   add_library(mmesh SHARED ${MMESH_SOURCES})
   target_include_directories(
     mmesh PUBLIC
     $<INSTALL_INTERFACE:${INCLUDE_DIR}>
     $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/../include>
   )
   target_link_libraries(mmesh PRIVATE ${MM_LIBS})
+  set_target_properties(mmesh PROPERTIES
+    VERSION   ${PROJECT_VERSION}
+    SOVERSION ${PROJECT_VERSION_MAJOR}
+  )
   set_property(TARGET mmesh APPEND PROPERTY COMPILE_DEFINITIONS "MMESH_DLL_EXPORTS")
   set_property(TARGET mmesh APPEND PROPERTY INTERFACE_COMPILE_DEFINITIONS "MMESH_DLL_IMPORTS")
   install(TARGETS mmesh
